{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection... reinfection working definition in this study was based on a positive laboratory result at least 90 days after laboratory confirmation of primary infection(laboratory testing methods include reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction or rapid antigen test, also called Lateral Flow Devices, and so on)... (4) Original research. The exclusion criteria were: (1) The sample size was less than 20; (2) Belonged to one of the following types of studies: editorial, case report, case series study, systematic review, meta-analysis, animal experiment, news report; (3) Secondary reporting or articles on repeated studies of the same population; (4) Grey literature, including a range of documents not controlled by commercial publishing organizations.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies many study-level eligibility characteristics (eligible designs, minimum sample size, reinfection definition, original research requirement, exclusions), but does not comprehensively report all study-characteristic components expected (for example explicit settings, detailed follow-up requirements, or a full question-framework/PICOS breakdown), so coverage is partial."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language. We conducted preliminary screening based on the English title and English abstract provided by nonEnglish articles. Further, in the screening process, if the included article was neither in English nor in Chinese and did not provide an English abstract or full text, we used an online translator (Google Translate) for translation. There were no non-English articles in the final articles included in this study... The exclusion criteria were: ... (4) Grey literature, including a range of documents not controlled by commercial publishing organizations.",
      "reason": "The review states language inclusion (no language limits and translation approach) and exclusion of grey literature, but does not report eligibility restrictions by dissemination year or explicit publication/report status beyond excluding grey literature, so the reporting of report-characteristic criteria is only partial."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": \"One of them reported only the reinfection rate, but not the associated number of first infections as well as the number of reinfections, and two other articles studied the same population, so the meta-analysis of single-group rates could not be performed. Therefore, we excluded the above literature with the number of unreported infections and selected one of two literature with the same population for inclusion.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript explicitly distinguishes and reports excluding studies that reported only rates but did not provide the underlying numbers (i.e., outcomes not reported), and excludes duplicates/same-population reports, demonstrating distinction between lack of reported outcome results and other exclusions."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": \"Subgroup analysis was also performed to obtain reinfection rates and forest plots according to age, variant, and country... Subgroup analyses were performed by meta-regression to fit stratified rates of reinfection based on variables such as variant and country, and we also used spline regression to fit time-varying reinfection rates...\",
      "reason": "The review specifies the groups used in syntheses (age, variant, country, study population, study type) and links these subgroup/meta-regression analyses to the objectives of estimating and comparing reinfection rates, so groups used in each synthesis are specified and connected to comparisons."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": \"first, we did not include the 'grey literature' , which may lack potential relevant studies that meet the inclusion criteria [35]. In addition, the pattern of publication bias in the field of single-arm study with single-group rate is not clear, and funnel plot analysis may lead to inaccurate conclusions.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript provides a rationale for at least one notable restriction (exclusion of grey literature), explaining concerns about quality and publication-bias implications; thus a rationale for a notable eligibility restriction is provided."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "85"
}

